# 14. Dockerfile

Dockerfile defines how to build an image.

Example:

```dockerfile
FROM nginx

COPY index.html /usr/share/nginx/html

EXPOSE 80
```

---

## Dockerfile Instructions

## FROM

Base image.

Example:

```dockerfile
FROM ubuntu
```

---

## RUN

Execute commands during image creation.

Example:

```dockerfile
RUN apt update
```

---

## COPY

Copy files.

Example:

```dockerfile
COPY app.jar /app/
```

---

## WORKDIR

Set working directory.

Example:

```dockerfile
WORKDIR /app
```

---

## EXPOSE

Documents application port.

Example:

```dockerfile
EXPOSE 8080
```

---

## CMD

Default command.

Example:

```dockerfile
CMD ["java","-jar","app.jar"]
```

