# 21. Docker Volumes

Containers are temporary.

Example:

```text
Container deleted

↓

Data deleted
```

Volumes provide persistent storage.

---

Create volume:

```bash
docker volume create data-volume
```

Use volume:

```bash
docker run \
-v data-volume:/data \
mysql
```

---

# 22. Docker Networking

Containers communicate through networks.

List networks:

```bash
docker network ls
```

---

Create network:

```bash
docker network create app-network
```

---

Run container:

```bash
docker run \
--network app-network \
